WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.420
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:06.180
At some point, I’m sure many of you have
seen a list of the famously non-relevant interview

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:08.120
questions asked at Google.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:12.419
Things like “How much would you charge to
wash every window in Seattle?”

00:00:12.419 --> 00:00:16.840
This is obviously a stupid question because
no one would pay you as it never stops raining

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.390
in Seattle, like…ever.

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:24.630
Another question on the list is this: Imagine
a country where everyone only wants boys so

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:28.060
if a couple have a girl, they have another
child.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.349
If they have a boy, they stop.

00:00:30.349 --> 00:00:35.000
What is the proportion of boys to girls in
the country?

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.350
A difficult question, and there’s a lot
of debate over the correct answer, but most

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:44.260
people come to the conclusion that the answer
is a 50/50 mix of boys and girls.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:50.690
But what we want to ask today is; do you really
have a 50/50 chance of having a boy or a girl?

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:54.390
Are there any genetic or environmental factors
that can affect it?

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:59.899
And, is there really such a black and white,
or should I say blue and pink, difference

00:00:59.899 --> 00:01:01.699
between the genders?

00:01:01.699 --> 00:01:06.320
So in the words of some woman who likes to
stick meat on her dresses, why was I born

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:11.920
this way?

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:18.040
Humans have 23 pairs of chromosomes and 22
pairs are the same for men and women.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:23.300
The 23rd pair though are the sex chromosomes
and women have two X ones, whereas men have

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:27.670
an X and a Y, where the Y is much smaller
than the X.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:32.649
The X chromosome has over 2000 genes in it
while the Y has just 78.

00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:37.369
But before you start thinking that women have
cheated by sneaking in a few thousand extra

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:42.979
genes to play with; very soon after fertilization,
one of the pair of X genes in women almost

00:01:42.979 --> 00:01:48.650
completely deactivates so we all end up with
a similar number.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:54.110
For the first few weeks as a fetus, male and
females are basically the same.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:02:00.189
Then, the genitals go their separate directions
but although we see the equipment down there

00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:04.119
as being very different, it’s more similar
than you think.

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:10.850
The gonads become either testes or ovaries,
the phallus becomes either a penis or a clitoris,

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:14.420
which actually extends a few inches, it’s
just internal.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:20.470
And the labia and scrotum are pretty similar
bits of skin, just with a different…

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:23.640
um… let’s say; origami.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:28.800
It takes until the 16th week of pregnancy
or later, when we can peer in and see what

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:36.280
sex a baby is and realise that we have to
return all the pink dresses we bought.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:41.020
So when you see how genitalia develop, you
realize that it’s possible that they may

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:46.840
not develop fully in one direction, since
they start as pretty similar stuff.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:56.370
Depending on the definition, between 0.1%
and 1.7% of people are born biologically “intersex”

00:02:56.370 --> 00:03:01.980
since their anatomy doesn’t fall strictly
into one category or the other, it lands somewhere

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:02.980
in the middle.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:07.160
It’s also possible to have XX and XY chromosomes.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:11.390
There’s even a very rare condition where
the Y chromosome gets tagged on to one of

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.310
the XX chromosomes.

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:18.630
Many of these outcomes are rare because it’s
very likely they won’t be able to reproduce,

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.690
so the characteristics don’t get passed
on.

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:27.200
If only the same could be true for people
who recline their seat on planes; I think

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.620
we would all like the seat recliner gene to
be deleted from the population.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:35.250
Alright, that’s the development part and
all the dangly bits out of the way.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:41.300
But how do the cells of ‘you’ initially
settle on their XX or XY combination?

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:45.150
Do the sperm and egg arm wrestle for it?

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:48.530
If you hang a picture of Vin Diesel above
the bed does this increase your chances of

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:50.180
having a boy?

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:56.290
Right now, globally, the sex ratio is 107
boys for every 100 girls.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.640
The gender is decided by the sperm.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:03.700
A man produces 2 different sperm cells; one
contains an X chromosome and the other contains

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:09.580
a Y chromosome so if the X fertilizes the
egg, you get a girl and if it’s the Y, it’s

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:10.580
a boy.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:13.330
If it’s the Z chromosome then you get a
wizard, congratulations.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:18.220
As the X and Y contain different amount of
genes, like we mentioned before, this means

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:24.510
that the X sperm is actually 1.03 times heavier
than the Y.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:30.740
The Y sperm is known to be more mobile but
the X has a longer lifespan so it’s possible,

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:36.950
although not proven, that increased gravitational
pressure during and just after sex, could

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:40.110
have some influence on the baby’s gender.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:44.150
So make sure try sitting a bit differently
if you’ve already engraved “Jessica”

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.730
onto the crib.

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:50.840
There are many myths out there about how you
can influence the gender outcome, from what

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:56.210
point of ovulation you have sex at, to the
type of breakfast cereal you eat, but nothing

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:58.490
reliable has ever been proven.

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:04.150
The reason almost all species end up with
a 1:1 sex ratio is down to a thing called

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.920
Fisher’s Principle.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:10.840
Imagine there are less male births than female,
this would mean that a newborn male will have

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:13.940
more people to mate with than a new born female.

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:18.070
So any parents that have a tendency to produce
males will end up with more grandchildren.

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:23.940
But then this tendency will spread and soon
the ratio will change so the benefit of producing

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:25.490
males stops.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:32.200
It’s really only colony species such as
ants and bees where this ratio doesn’t apply.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:37.220
In bees, it’s controlled by a fertilized
egg being female and an unfertilized one being

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.220
male.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:43.220
Females who are not destined for the queenhood
are also fed a restricted diet so their reproductive

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:44.610
organs don’t develop.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:50.500
It’s the same reason why Prince Harry was
fed exclusively on pop tarts, poor lad.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:55.290
Fisher’s Principle is just a natural balancing
act but, surprisingly, there are environmental

00:05:55.290 --> 00:06:00.830
factors that can alter the human sex ratio
for the population in an area.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:06.360
Ralph Catalano, a Berkley professor, published
a report that said the ambient temperature

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:16.470
would change the ratio and a 1 °C rise would
create 1 in 1000 extra boys.

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:21.320
Another well-established phenomenon is that
after a war, the birth rate of males noticeably

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:26.430
increases, as if the great galactic accountant
is trying to balance the books.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.680
But how is this possible?

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:33.000
Our genes can’t see all that extra space
around the locker room and think “right,

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.830
it’s man-making time”.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:41.480
Well, Dr Corry Gellatly suspects it’s still
all down to the Fisher Principle.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:46.840
If you are a man from a family with more brothers
than sisters that means you probably produce

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:51.470
more Y sperm than X; you’re a man-making-machine.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:57.350
If you family is mostly sisters, then you’ve
likely got more X sperm; you’re a female

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:58.520
factory.

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:02.730
When a major war comes and all the men get
shipped out to battle, a family with more

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:08.420
brothers has a greater chance of having at
least one son return alive, so there is a

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:13.860
bigger proportion of Y-sperm bias in the lads
who finally return when the war is over.

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:17.430
That’s all life is really; sperm and statistics.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:22.380
Of course, no matter what the sex of a new
born baby, over their lifetime, they are going

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:29.580
to produce about 600 large cans of garbage
and over 10 million liters of waste water.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:34.480
So maybe there are enough Dave’s and Sarah’s
in the world, and I wouldn’t mind finding

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:38.650
a seat on the train every now and then, so
perhaps you should just adopt a cat instead.

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:53.930
Thanks for the view, subscribe for more Thoughty2.

